  ],
  "text": "There may be a quantum compass inside a robin's eye. Every compass you have ever used needed a needle. This one does not. A protein in the retina reacts when a magnetic field passes through it. And the reaction depends on which direction the bird is facing. Which means direction may arrive as part of what the bird sees. Sea turtles do it too. So do salmon, and they use it as a map. So the shield that stops the solar wind is also a navigation system. Life found it and learned to read it long before we knew it was there. There is a sense you do not have, running right over your head all day. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
